# What always goes through WireGuard, also while the tunnel is in Claude only.
# One entry per line: an address range (a.b.c.d/n) or a name, which covers its
# subdomains too. A site on shared addresses (Cloudflare) goes in by name.
# After a change: vpn-setup (sudo). `vpn-hosts ranges|names` prints what it reads.

160.79.104.0/23  # Anthropic: api.anthropic.com, claude.ai, platform.claude.com
openrouter.ai    # 403 without the tunnel; the API is on the same name
api.moonshot.ai  # asked for 2026-10-13; direct it answers 401 without a key, so not proven
# YouTube in a browser, seen 2026-10-15: no connection without the tunnel, and the ISP's
# resolver answers NXDOMAIN for youtube.com. jnn-pa.googleapis.com works direct.
youtube.com                # www, m, music, s
googlevideo.com            # the video itself
youtubei.googleapis.com    # the player's API
ytimg.com                  # thumbnails (i.ytimg.com)
yt3.ggpht.com              # avatars
yt4.ggpht.com
yt3.googleusercontent.com  # channel art
youtube-nocookie.com       # embeds on other sites
ikea.com                   # 403 on www.ikea.com without the tunnel (2026-10-16); photos on the same name
